{{Top|notoc=1}}
{{Youmay|the astronomical term|[[the galaxy]] that contained worlds such as [[Tatooine]] and [[Coruscant]]}}
[[File:GalaxyMap_JediArchives.png|thumb|right|250px|A map showing both the main galaxy (Center) and its satellite galaxies, the Rishi Maze (Top-Left) and the far galaxy (Bottom-Right)]]
A '''galaxy''' was a massive collection of [[star]]s, [[star system]]s, [[planet]]s, [[moon]]s, [[asteroid]]s, [[comet]]s, [[nebula]]s, [[star cluster]]s, [[black hole]]s, and other celestial bodies residing within the [[universe]]. 

==Description==
One known galaxy was [[the galaxy]] home to the [[Galactic Republic]]<ref name="Episode I">{{Film|I}}</ref> and the [[Galactic Empire]],<ref name="Episode III">{{Film|III}}</ref> also notable for containing the [[Wellspring of Life]] which gave birth to the [[midi-chlorian]]s.<ref name="TCWDestiny">{{TCW|Destiny (The Clone Wars)}}</ref> Some galaxies had smaller, companion galaxies that orbited them. The galaxy had at least two,<ref name="Star Wars: Episode II Attack of the Clones">{{Film|II}}</ref> the [[Rishi Maze]]<ref name="SWE-Kamino">{{SWE|locations|kamino|Kamino}}</ref> and the [[far galaxy]].

According to [[Huyang]], the space whales known as the [[purrgil]] were capable of [[Intergalactic travel|traveling]] across different galaxies using intergalactic hyperspace lanes. These lanes were known to the [[Jedi Order]], which preserved information about them inside the [[Jedi Archives]].<ref name="Ahsoka 3">{{Ahsoka|Part Three: Time to Fly}}</ref> Between galaxies sat the [[intergalactic void]].<ref name="Part 4">{{Ahsoka|Part Four: Fallen Jedi}}</ref> The so-called [[far galaxy]] contained the planet [[Peridea]], which was regarded as a fairy tale by [[Jedi]] such as [[Baylan Skoll]] but as history by the [[Nightsisters|Nightsister]] [[Morgan Elsbeth]]. Beings from this distant galaxy built a [[Seatos reflex point|reflex point]] on the planet [[Seatos]] which was used to point the [[Pathway to Peridea|pathway]] to Peridea.<ref name="Ahsoka 2">{{Ahsoka|Part Two: Toil and Trouble}}</ref>

==History==
[[File:Pathway_to_peridea.png|thumb|left|250px|The pathway to Peridea]]
[[Taka Jamoreesa]], when advertising themselves as a [[pilot]], was said to be "wanted" in eighteen galaxies.<ref name="Last Shot">''[[Last Shot]]''</ref>

In the hands of [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]], the [[Mustafarian]] [[Bright Star]] artifact had the capability to crumble entire galaxies, where the [[Sith Lord]] would sacrifice their [[Living Force|vitality]] in his insatiable hunger.<ref name="ImmortalII">{{VaderImmortal|II}}</ref>

During the [[Liberation of Lothal]], a pod of purrgil took [[Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn]] and the [[Jedi]] rebel [[Ezra Bridger]] to Peridea. Ten years later, during the time of the [[New Republic]], [[Morgan Elsbeth]] commissioned the construction of a massive [[Hyperspace transport ring|hyperspace ring]] known as the ''[[Eye of Sion]]'' in order to bring Thrawn back to the known galaxy.<ref name="Ahsoka 2" /> [[Ahsoka Tano]] also discovered a [[star map]] at a [[Nightsisters' Temple|former Nightsister stronghold]] on [[Arcana]], which provided a map to Peridea's galaxy. [[Sabine Wren]] managed to unlock the map but it was stolen by [[Shin Hati]], an agent of Elsbeth.<ref name="Ahsoka 1">{{Ahsoka|Part One: Master and Apprentice}}</ref>

Following a [[Incident on Seatos|duel]] with Tano and Wren on Seatos, [[Baylan Skoll]] managed to unlock the star map and relay the coordinates for the [[pathway to Peridea]] to Elsbeth. Elsbeth's forces then departed on the ''Eye of Sion'' with the captive Wren to Peridea.<ref name="Ahsoka 4">{{Ahsoka|Part Four: Fallen Jedi}}</ref> Using the pathway, Elsbeth's forces reached Peridea where they established contact with the [[Great Mother]]s and Thrawn's forces.<ref name="Ahsoka 6">{{Ahsoka|Part Six: Far, Far Away}}</ref> They then spent the next three cycles loading caskets from the catacombs beneath the [[Great Mothers' Fortress]].<ref name="Ahsoka 8">{{Ahsoka|Part Eight: The Jedi, the Witch, and the Warlord}}</ref> 

Tano and [[Huyang]] subsequently traveled to the far galaxy with a [[purrgil]] pod and reunited with Wren and Bridger, who had become the leader of a [[Noti]] clan.<ref name="Ahsoka 7">{{Ahsoka|Part Seven: Dreams and Madness}}</ref> Following a skirmish with Tano, Wren and Bridger, Thrawn, the Great Mothers and his [[Star Destroyer]] ''[[Chimaera]]'' managed to [[Battle of Peridea|escape]] Peridea and return to their home galaxy using the ''Eye of Sion''. While Tano, Wren and Huyang were stranded on Peridea, Bridger managed to stow aboard the ''Chimaera'' and reunited with [[General]] [[Hera Syndulla]].<ref name="Ahsoka 8" />

